"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KCEM5PTM1S0MK7X\",\"title\":\"MobiChar x GA — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"MobiChar x GA\",\"Alcom Carbon Markets\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"S5SH\",\"Crediting period\",\"15 Feb 2026 to 14 Feb 2036\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"S5SH\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Jul 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://alcomsg.com\",\"t\":\"Alcom Carbon Markets\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1KC47RA0K1S0JZB7\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-requirements\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KOmLuhU6yzCYYtUWPyQCw4aByEEJ7Q1-/view\",\"t\":\"VVB Policy\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KC47RA0K1S0JZB7/prj_1KCEM5PTM1S0MK7X/pjd_1KWEHFT9K1S0PH1J/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nMobiChar x GA\\nAlcom Carbon Markets\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nS5SH\\nCrediting period\\n15 Feb 2026 to 14 Feb 2036\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nMobichar is Alcom's next generation of biochar projects - a truck mounted pyrolyzer that converts biomass into high quality biochar and bio-oil. Mobichar x GA is located in deep in the hinterlands of Maharashtra (India) and utilizes waste cotton stalks sourced from a network of small holder farmers via our project implementation partners.\\n\\nMaharashtra\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 10 Jul 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nAudit kick-off\\n\\nA Validation & Verification Body (VVB) officially commences the project validation and verification process. All VVBs are approved and appointed by Isometric based on the requirements outlined in the Isometric Standard and VVB Policy.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 Jul 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"